{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":851,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Ps.114","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Psalms","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Psalms 114","reference":"Psalms 114","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"This and the four following psalms, the Jews were wont to sing at the close of the paschal supper."},{"verse":2,"text":"It is a solemn commemoration of God's delivering Israel, giving them the law, and water out of the rock, ver."},{"verse":3,"text":"1-8."},{"verse":4,"text":"2.","scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":5,"text":"Judah - Or Israel, one tribe being put for all.","scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":6,"text":"Judah he mentions as the chief of all the tribes.","scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":7,"text":"4.","scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":8,"text":"The mountains - Horeb and Sinai, two tops of one mountain, and other neighbouring mountains.","scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":9,"text":"7.","scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":10,"text":"Tremble - The mountains did more than what was fit at the appearance of the great God.","scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Psalms","chapter":114}}